{
  "slug": "artist:juice-wrld",
  "name": "Juice WRLD",
  "editorial_article": "Born Jarad Higgins in Chicago, this artist became a pivotal figure in the emo rap and SoundCloud rap movements of the late 2010s. His 2018 diamond-certified single 'Lucid Dreams', produced by Nick Mira, peaked at number two on the Billboard Hot 100 and helped define his melodic, emotionally raw output. Influenced by artists as diverse as Billy Idol, Black Sabbath, and Kanye West, Higgins recorded his debut studio album 'Goodbye & Good Riddance' (2018) via Grade A Productions and Interscope. His second album, 'Death Race for Love' (2019), reached number one on the Billboard 200, featuring the hit 'Robbery'. Following his death from a drug overdose in December 2019, posthumous releases like 'Legends Never Die' and 'Fighting Demons' maintained his chart dominance, with 'Legends Never Die' matching records for most U.S. top-ten entries from a single album.",
